(2) Subject to the exceptions hereinafter specified, no Civil Court shall exercise jurisdiction as to any of the following matters, namely:--
(a) claims against the Government relating to any property appertaining to any office or for any service whatsoever;
(b) objections,-- (i) to the amount or incidence of any assessment of land revenue under this Act, or (ii) to the mode of assessment or levy, or to the principle on which such assessment or levy is fixed, or (iii) to the validity or effect of the notification of survey or settlement;
